

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 7

                                  FOR

                                  KAHN







          Lorenzo Cammoranesi
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  German philosopher George Hegel, 1821:
  "In England even the poorest of people believe they have Rights; this is 
very different from what satisfies the poor in other lands."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Stormy winter gave way to sweet spring.  Kahn attempted a Flood spell, but 
bungled it.
  Milo's Crossroads was magically blessed and prospered.  The skeletal 
remains of the 171st Phalanx were Blessed and permanently destroyed.
  In early summer, Kahn searched the Hollow Tree with the intention of 
overcoming it and whatever vile guardian beast lay within.  Kahn encountered 
the Centaur.  Kahn attempted to help his fortunes with a Mirror-Image 
Phantasm spell, but it sputtered at the last second.
  The Centaur loped along smoothly and closed to bow range.  Kahn thought to 
attempt a Fireball spell, but couldn't find a needed material component 
before Kahn could make his spellcast.  The Centaur fired an arrow at Kahn 
and inflicted 3 damage points on him.  The Centaur boldly fired an arrow at 
Kahn and damaged him, inflicting 2 damage points.
  Kahn charged into the melee.  The Centaur shifted over to a better 
defensive position.  Then the Centaur kicked at Kahn and inflicted 5 damage 
points.  Kahn staggered, stunned by the deadly blow.  And so it came to pass 
that Kahn met his tragic end.  He was succeeded by his next-in-line (who 
will use his predecessor's name until next turn).
  Kahn's will left all his possessions to his compatriots.  The heir of Kahn 
gained the Tome of Blessings.
  Kahn saw nothing special while scouting out the Hollow Tree.

  Hawkins's Oratory spell fizzled and Hawkins was left with his face covered 
with psycho-kinetic slime.  Sherwood was hit by a plague.  The plague struck 
the 143rd Light Cavalry in Sherwood and destroyed them.  The plague struck 
the 144th Legion in Sherwood and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 
214th Fleet in Sherwood and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 219th 
Legion in Sherwood and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 221st 
Light Cavalry in Sherwood and destroyed them.  Gladstone cast a Phantasmal 
Armies spell and illusory armies were formed for Kahn.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1)'s forces initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at Sherwood, a Forest province owing allegiance to Kahn.  
Guerin (#18) commanded the attacking armies.  The defending forces were 
commanded by Kahn.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown 
here:

