  DEFENDING ARMY

  Guerin led his armies into the fray.  Standing tall with his warriors was 
Kahn.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The army of Kahn used magic to aid their cause.  Magical 
phantasmal armies fought with hiss soldiers.  A bad omen appeared, which 
dealt a severe blow to Guerin (#18)'s hopes.  Guerin's mount was shot and 
killed from under Guerin.  On the other hand Guerin maneuvered his forces 
against Kahn with excellent tactical foresight and consequently enjoyed a 
tremendous tactical advantage.
  Kahn's troops were prepared to struggle like tigers for their fatherland.
  Out on the right outside flank, the Elite 240th Bowmen were encouraged to 
berserk fanatiscm by Guerin, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They 
faced the 218th Legion, who were blessed by a retinue of priests sent by the 
League of Pagan Clerics, which inspired them to a fanatical fury.  In this 
sector, the 240th Bowmen's commander cleverly unleashed a herd of 
pink-painted elephants to make his opponents imagine they were going crazy, 
but the ruse had little effect except to amuse them.  The 240th Bowmen 
battled the 218th Legion and fought them to a standstill.
  In the interior lines, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed 
against the 184th Bowmen.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on the 
188th Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons were 
decimated by the bolts fired by the dangerous Bowmen.  The 277th Eagles 
swooped down on the 184th Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  The 277th 
Eagles were riddled with fire of their dangerous Bowmen enemy.  On this 
battleground, the commander of the 184th Bowmen was flattened by a boulder 
thrown from a catapult, which greatly deflated the spirits of the troops.
  But the battle was not yet over.  The regimental band of the 108th 
Skeletal Bowmen was squashed by a boulder hurled from a catapult, which 
greatly deflated the spirits of the troops.  Still, the 108th Skeletal 
Bowmen fought with the 184th Bowmen and gradually shoved them back.
  Out on the left wing, the Crack 110th Bowmen were encouraged to selfless 
fanatiscm by Guerin, their revered First Elder of Elvenkind.  They were 
arrayed against the Crack 142nd Legion.  Here, the cowardice of a soldier 
worked against the 142nd Legion.  They were thrown into disarray when he 
panicked and ran, shouting "The battle is hopeless!  We're all cooked!"  The 
110th Bowmen fought with the 142nd Legion and battled them tooth and nail, 
neither side willing to give ground.
  Guerin's armies vanquished the army opposing them with a final charge.  
The 108th Skeletal Bowmen destroyed the 184th Bowmen.  The 124th Skeletal 
Dragons overtook the enemy in their headlong retreat and slew the 142nd 
Legion almost to a man.  The 277th Eagles chased after the enemy and were 
beaten off by the 218th Legion in a tough rearguard action.
  Sherwood was overrun by the forces of Guerin.  The battle affected the 
quality of our forces:  the 218th Legion had its morale shaken by a bad omen 
which manifested itself before the battle.  The 218th Legion has slipped in 
quality and now it's a Green unit.  Kahn retreated to Quantara Roo with what 
remained of his forces.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Kahn for this year.


  Kahn treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Kahn treated with his ally 
Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3).  Kahn treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Kahn 
treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Kahn treated with his ally 
Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Kahn treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Kahn treated 
with his ally Agesilao (#9).
  Quantara Roo was plundered by the Imp, who stormed from out of the dark 
wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 1 gold worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Kahn's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 17 gold in revenue.  11 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  
The 218th Legion trained well and improved in quality.  7 gold was expended 
to maintain our armies.  Kahn was left with 18 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Hume
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I was tutored in Druidism by Ishtar.  I practiced my Druidism 
and improved substantially.
  With the coming of the early summer season I moved into Orielle.  To the 
northeast lies a Desert area called Marzuq (#303), populated by Humans.  It 
is ruled by Prometeo.  Their Human warriors traditionally fight as 
Camel Corps.  East of here lies the poor province of Shasta (#304), ruled by 
no one.  It is known to be a Mountain province inhabited by Eagles.  They 
can call on an army of Eagles to defend their province.  Viewing the 
northwestern horizon, a man can see a poor Mountain province called Tesawa 
(#203).  It is said that Prometeo reigns there.  It is known to be occupied 
by Humans.  Their Human fighters array themselves in the style of Legion.  I 
saw no marauding monsters.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  I failed in my 
ineffectual attempt to cast a Resurrection spell.
  During fall, I rode into Macondo.  I was informed by some sheepherders of 
a perilous feature in Macondo, a Monastery (#114) inhabited by the Genie.  
What treasure may lie there is unknown.  Legend-keepers revere the Genie as 
a good, powerful spirit capable of such magical feats as flying, using some 
of the five magical abilities amd they may sometimes even grant a wish.  I 
saw no monster.
  During early winter, I could not cast a Bless spell because I had already 
cast my allowed number of White Magic spells.  Instead, in my sagely 
researches, I discovered a fabulous invention called the Macadam Roads!  The 
following benefits are conferred by the Macadam Roads:
  Macadam Roads are an improvement over the old dirt roads because they 
drain well and troops never get bogged down in mud, so they can move faster. 
Their effect is to raise the March ability of all of the characters of the 
Kingdom by 1 level.


  Thy humble servant,   Hume


From: Charious
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a Part Sea spell and the waters of Mammoth were 
magically parted.
  With the advent of the early summer season I travelled to Sherwood.  
During my travels this season, a Renegade Priest came at me like a bolt from 
the blue.  I spoke to the Renegade Priest with respectful words, and a fight 
was averted.

  Midsummer's day passed and a pleasant late summer came.  Gladstone was 
resurrected by the spell cast by me.
  During fall, I could not use magic item 3304 to cast a spell because I 
didn't own it.  I tried to improve my Sageness, but the task was beyond my 
natural aptitude.  I invented nothing worthy of note in my sagely 
experiments.
  With the advent of the early winter season I was tutored in Illusions by 
Gladstone.  I practiced well and improved my ability in Illusions.

  Thy humble servant,   Charious


From: Frodo, Squire to Hawkins
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into sweet spring.  Hawkins spoke urgently to Fingol of the 
greatness of Kahn's empire and convinced Fingol to pledge his allegiance to 
Kahn.  After talking to Fingol, Hawkins judged him (a Human well known for 
Tactics) to have a Druidic, Berserk character.
  In early summer, Hawkins journeyed to Sherwood.  During his travels, 
Hawkins was ambushed, pinned down and severely beaten by angry vigilantes.  
Hawkins finally broke free.  A Royal Ranger caught up with Hawkins.  But 
when he was taken to the local sheriff, he showed him the official seal of 
Kahn, and was let go.

  With the advent of the late summer season, Hawkins's Oratory spell fizzled 
and Hawkins was left with his face covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  In fall, Hawkins was instructed in Tactics by Fingol.  Hawkins practiced 
his Tactics and his skill in Tactics went up.
  With the coming of the early winter season, Hawkins was tutored in the art 
of Illusions by Gladstone.  Hawkins practiced for months and his skill in 
Illusions increased.

  Thy humble servant,   Frodo, Squire to Hawkins


From: Tonto, Squire to Fingol
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Windy spring blossomed into a sultry early summer.  Fingol rode into 
Peachwood.  To the west there lies a Forest province known as Ravenwood 
(#1102), a poor land of Humans where York reigns.  Their Human warriors 
array themselves as Legion and Fleet.  While adventuring, Fingol saw no 
monsters.
  In late summer, Fingol travelled to Sherwood.  Fingol saw no marauding 
monster.
  With the coming of the fall season, Fingol worked on his Tactics but was 
frustrated in his self-improvement efforts.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  Fingol was tutored in 
Illusions by Gladstone.  Fingol practiced well and improved his skill in 
Illusions.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Fingol


From: Gladstone
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In fall, I cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were formed 
for Kahn.
  The fall darkened into the stillness of early winter.  I tried to practice 
my Illusions, but the task was beyond my natural aptitude.

  Thy humble servant,   Gladstone


